  "details": "As has been well known for a long time, the default safety level that users have when they first get onto the platform is insufficient to protect users against being crashed by avatars, especially on the Quest platform.\nThe culprit is typically lights and particles, shaders and audio, all of which are not necessary for an enjoyable time on the platform, but when turned off make one’s experience better, especially on Quest.\nI think the normal safety shield should turn those off across the board, from visitors to trusted users. At least until such a time as VRChat secures their platform against avatar-based crashing methods.",
